Graphics were extracted from DMI containers, normalized into editable
PNG/TOML source, and packed without lossy conversion into native PNG atlases.
Existing Ogg audio was copied byte-for-byte. Tracker modules were rendered to
48 kHz stereo Ogg Vorbis with FFmpeg/libopenmpt. Exact source/output hashes and
transform metadata are stored under assets/upstream/goon and
assets/runtime/goon.

The first-party 192×192 station scenario adapts the pinned
`maps/atlas.dmm` crop at X 61–252, Y 61–252, Z 1 into native JSON. The import
flips source Y, maps a reviewed subset of areas, structures, utilities,
fixtures, and job landmarks, and records unsupported/omitted placements in the
scenario provenance. Sim Station does not execute DM or load DMM at runtime.

The project currently relies on Goonstation's root license for audio files
without stronger per-file evidence, as requested by the project owner. That
accepted risk and the takedown process are documented in
docs/legal/audio-rights-risk.md.
